Money is reserved. Admin checks, approves, processes the actual payment and records its reference. Rejected requests return the reserved amount to the available wallet.

One important thing before launching real payments:

The 90-minute automatic approval means SWAS TASKS becomes responsible for paying that reward even if an administrator has not checked it. You should only publish tasks with rewards that your platform can actually fund, and for tasks sourced from GWENO, confirm the task is authorized and the reward conditions have genuinely been met. The wallet must not be funded by imaginary earnings or by assuming a third-party task provider has paid you.

**This prompt is designed to build the complete system in your existing SWAS TASKS project—not just the dashboard appearance.**